# **12. DP vs. TD**

| **Backup**               | **DP (Full Backup)**                                      | **TD (Sampled Backup)**                                  |
|--------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| **Information Used**     | Uses **all** possible transitions (summing over \(s'\))   | Uses **one** real transition \((S_t, A_t, R_{t+1}, S_{t+1})\) |
| **Requires a Model?**    | **Yes**, \(P(s'|s,a)\) and \(R(s,a)\)                     | **No**, learned from data (model-free)                   |
| **Computational Cost**   | High for large state spaces                               | More scalable                                           |

- **TD = “sample-based approach”:**
  - It backs up using real samples from experience.
  - It allows handling **large environments** without enumerating every state.

